#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4
msgid "3.x Changelog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:12
msgid ""
"Add a flag ``lifespan`` to :func:`~litestar.handlers.asgi`, defaulting to "
"``False``. When set to ``True``, the ASGI lifespan protocol will be ran for "
"the handler, after the host app's ``on_startup`` hooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:19
msgid ""
"Add a ``copy_state`` flag to :func:`~litestar.handlers.asgi`, defaulting to "
"``False``. It works similar to ``copy_scope``, and, if set, the mounted "
"application will receive a shallow copy of ``scope[\"state\"]``, so values "
"it sets there are not seen by the outer application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:43
msgid ""
"Add :attr:`~litestar.params.ParameterKwarg.documentation_only`. If set, the "
"constraints of a parameter are included in the OpenAPI schema, but not "
"applied to the value of a request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:72
msgid ""
"Deprecate :class:`~litestar.datastructures.Headers`, :data:`~litestar.params.QueryParams`, :data:`~litestar.params.RequestCookies`, "
"and :data:`~litestar.types.Scope` as request parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:77
msgid ""
":class:`~litestar.connection.ASGIConnection`\\ 's ``headers``, "
"``query_params``, ``cookies``, or ``scope`` attributes should be used "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:111
msgid ""
"Drop the special meaning of the \"reserved keyword arguments\" in handlers "
"and DI providers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:114
msgid ""
"The parameter names can now freely be used and assigned, as their meaning is "
"derived from their respective annotation:"
msgstr ""

