#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:600
msgid ""
":class:`~litestar.middleware.session.base.SessionMiddleware` has been moved "
"from the legacy ``AbstractMiddleware`` base "
"to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, as part of migrating all "
"built-in middleware off the legacy bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:604
msgid ""
"The middleware still takes a session backend, which keeps receiving its "
"configuration unchanged, but no longer wraps an ``app``. The ``middleware`` "
"property "
"of :class:`~litestar.middleware.session.server_side.ServerSideSessionConfig` "
"and :class:`~litestar.middleware.session.client_side.CookieBackendConfig` "
"now returns a ``SessionMiddleware`` instance instead of a "
"``DefineMiddleware`` wrapping it, so applications using "
"``middleware=[session_config.middleware]`` are unaffected. Code that "
"constructed the middleware directly, or introspected the "
"``DefineMiddleware``, must be updated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:614
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"middleware = SessionMiddleware(app=next_app, backend=backend)\n"
"backend = session_config.middleware.kwargs[\"backend\"]\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"middleware = SessionMiddleware(backend=backend)\n"
"asgi_app = middleware(next_app)\n"
"backend = session_config.middleware.backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:624
msgid ""
"The new ``exclude_path_pattern`` option of the session configurations "
"matches against the handler's path (e.g. ``/user/{user_id:int}``); handlers "
"excluded this way, or via ``exclude_opt_key``, bypass the middleware "
"entirely at startup rather than per request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:629
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:892
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:929
msgid ""
"Since ``ASGIMiddleware.__call__`` returns a closure rather than the "
"middleware instance, a middleware stack can no longer be introspected by "
"walking the ``.app`` attribute of each layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:634
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:897
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:934
msgid ":ref:`asgi-middleware-migration`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:642
msgid ""
"``PrometheusMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy "
"``AbstractMiddleware`` base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, "
"as part of migrating all built-in middleware off the legacy bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:646
msgid ""
"Since the middleware is now directly constructible, "
"the :class:`~litestar.plugins.prometheus.PrometheusConfig` configuration "
"object is obsolete and its ``middleware`` property is deprecated; it will be "
"removed in ``4.0``. Pass a configured ``PrometheusMiddleware`` instance to "
"the middleware list instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:653
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"config = PrometheusConfig(app_name=\"my-app\", group_path=True)\n"
"app = Litestar(..., middleware=[config.middleware])\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"app = Litestar(\n"
"    ...,\n"
"    middleware=[PrometheusMiddleware(app_name=\"my-app\", "
"group_path=True)],\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:664
msgid ""
"Subclasses of ``PrometheusMiddleware`` must rename ``__call__`` to "
"``handle``, which receives the next ASGI app as an additional ``next_app`` "
"argument in place of ``self.app``, and read settings from the corresponding "
"instance attributes instead of the removed private ``self._config``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:669
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:707
msgid ""
"``exclude`` patterns are still matched against the request path. The new "
"``exclude_path_pattern`` argument matches against the handler's path (e.g. "
"``/user/{user_id:int}``) instead; handlers excluded this way, or via "
"``exclude_opt_key``, bypass the middleware entirely at startup rather than "
"per request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:675
msgid ""
"Mounted ASGI apps stay wrapped regardless of the configured ``scopes``, with "
"their connections filtered by scope type at runtime, so restricting the "
"middleware to e.g. ``{\"websocket\"}`` also holds for connections through "
"mounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:685
msgid ""
"``RateLimitMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy "
"``AbstractMiddleware`` base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, "
"as part of migrating all built-in middleware off the legacy bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:689
msgid ""
"Since the middleware is now directly constructible, "
"the :class:`~litestar.middleware.rate_limit.RateLimitConfig` configuration "
"object is obsolete and its ``middleware`` property is deprecated; it will be "
"removed in ``4.0``. Pass a configured ``RateLimitMiddleware`` instance to "
"the middleware list instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:696
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"config = RateLimitConfig(rate_limit=(\"minute\", 10), exclude=[\"/"
"schema\"])\n"
"app = Litestar(..., middleware=[config.middleware])\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"app = Litestar(\n"
"    ...,\n"
"    middleware=[RateLimitMiddleware(rate_limit=(\"minute\", 10), exclude=[\"/"
"schema\"])],\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:719
msgid ""
"Add support for ``leeway`` parameter in JWT security backends, which allows "
"set a number of potential seconds as a clock error for expired tokens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:722
msgid ""
"``Token.decode`` and ``Token.decode_payload`` now take a ``leeway`` "
"argument. Custom token classes overriding either method must accept it and "
"forward to ``super()``, otherwise decoding raises ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:742
msgid ""
"Exceeding the configured multipart form part limit now returns ``413 Request "
"Entity Too Large`` instead of ``400 Bad Request``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:750
msgid ""
"The ``RapidocRenderPlugin`` has been removed due to lack of upstream "
"maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:752
msgid ""
"Applications using ``RapidocRenderPlugin`` should migrate to another bundled "
"UI plugin, such as ``ScalarRenderPlugin`` (the default), "
"``SwaggerRenderPlugin``, ``RedocRenderPlugin`` or ``StoplightRenderPlugin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:762
msgid ""
"``AllowedHostsMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy "
"``AbstractMiddleware`` base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, "
"as part of migrating all built-in middleware off the legacy bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:766
msgid ""
"Applications that configure allowed hosts "
"through :class:`~litestar.config.allowed_hosts.AllowedHostsConfig` or the "
"``allowed_hosts`` argument are unaffected, since Litestar constructs the "
"middleware itself. The constructor takes keyword arguments now instead of an "
"``app`` and an ``AllowedHostsConfig``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:773
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"middleware = AllowedHostsMiddleware(app=next_app, config=config)\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"middleware = AllowedHostsMiddleware(\n"
"    allowed_hosts=config.allowed_hosts,\n"
"    exclude=config.exclude,\n"
"    exclude_opt_key=config.exclude_opt_key,\n"
"    scopes=config.scopes,\n"
"    www_redirect=config.www_redirect,\n"
")\n"
"asgi_app = middleware(next_app)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:787
msgid ""
":attr:`~litestar.config.allowed_hosts.AllowedHostsConfig.exclude` patterns "
"are still matched against the request path. The "
"new :attr:`~litestar.config.allowed_hosts.AllowedHostsConfig.exclude_path_pattern` "
"matches against the handler's path (e.g. ``/user/{user_id:int}``) instead; "
"handlers excluded this way, or via ``exclude_opt_key``, bypass the "
"middleware entirely at startup rather than per request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:800
msgid ""
"``CompressionMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy "
"``AbstractMiddleware`` base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, "
"as part of migrating all built-in middleware off the legacy bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:804
msgid ""
"Applications that configure compression "
"through :class:`~litestar.config.compression.CompressionConfig` are "
"unaffected, since Litestar constructs the middleware itself. The middleware "
"still takes the ``CompressionConfig`` - which the ``CompressionFacade`` "
"protocol continues to receive unchanged - but no longer wraps an ``app``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:811
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"middleware = CompressionMiddleware(app=next_app, config=config)\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"middleware = CompressionMiddleware(config=config)\n"
"asgi_app = middleware(next_app)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:819
msgid ""
"Subclasses set "
"via :attr:`~litestar.config.compression.CompressionConfig.middleware_class` "
"must rename ``__call__`` to ``handle``, which receives the next ASGI app as "
"an additional ``next_app`` argument in place of ``self.app``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:824
msgid ""
":attr:`~litestar.config.compression.CompressionConfig.exclude` patterns are "
"still matched against the request path. The "
"new :attr:`~litestar.config.compression.CompressionConfig.exclude_path_pattern` "
"matches against the handler's path (e.g. ``/user/{user_id:int}``) instead; "
"handlers excluded this way, or via ``exclude_opt_key``, bypass the "
"middleware entirely at startup rather than per request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:837
msgid ""
"``CSRFMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy ``MiddlewareProtocol`` "
"base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, as part of migrating "
"all built-in middleware off the legacy bases. It now lives in "
"``litestar.middleware._internal``. This removes the "
"``litestar.middleware.csrf`` module, including the ``generate_csrf_token`` "
"and ``generate_csrf_hash`` helpers, from the public API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:843
msgid ""
"Applications that configure CSRF protection "
"through :class:`~litestar.config.csrf.CSRFConfig` are unaffected, since "
"Litestar constructs the middleware itself, via a ``from_config`` classmethod "
"on the middleware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:848
msgid ""
":attr:`~litestar.config.csrf.CSRFConfig.exclude` patterns are still matched "
"against the request path. The "
"new :attr:`~litestar.config.csrf.CSRFConfig.exclude_path_pattern` matches "
"against the handler's path (e.g. ``/user/{user_id:int}``) instead; handlers "
"excluded this way, or via ``exclude_from_csrf``, bypass the middleware "
"entirely at startup rather than per request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:861
msgid ""
"``ResponseCacheMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy "
"``AbstractMiddleware`` base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, "
"as part of migrating all built-in middleware off the legacy bases. It now "
"lives in ``litestar.middleware._internal``, removing it from the public API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:867
msgid ""
"The move into ``litestar.middleware._internal`` does not affect usage: the "
"middleware was only ever applied internally by Litestar to begin with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:870
msgid ""
"Applications that configure response caching "
"through :class:`~litestar.config.response_cache.ResponseCacheConfig` and the "
"handler-level ``cache`` argument are unaffected -- Litestar constructs the "
"middleware itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:874
msgid ""
"Code composing the middleware directly into an ASGI stack must drop the "
"``app`` argument, pass the settings as keyword arguments rather than a "
"``ResponseCacheConfig``, and apply the instance to the next ASGI app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:879
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"middleware = ResponseCacheMiddleware(app=next_app, "
"config=response_cache_config)\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"middleware = ResponseCacheMiddleware(\n"
"    default_expiration=response_cache_config.default_expiration,\n"
"    key_builder=response_cache_config.key_builder,\n"
"    store=response_cache_config.store,\n"
"    cache_response_filter=response_cache_config.cache_response_filter,\n"
")\n"
"asgi_app = middleware(next_app)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:905
msgid ""
"``CORSMiddleware`` has been moved from the legacy ``AbstractMiddleware`` "
"base to :class:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware`, as part of migrating "
"all built-in middleware off the legacy bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:909
msgid ""
"Applications that configure CORS "
"through :class:`~litestar.config.cors.CORSConfig` are unaffected -- Litestar "
"constructs the middleware itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:913
msgid ""
"Code instantiating the middleware directly must drop the ``app`` argument, "
"pass the settings as keyword arguments rather than a ``CORSConfig``, and "
"apply the instance to the next ASGI app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:918
msgid ""
"# before\n"
"middleware = CORSMiddleware(app=next_app, config=cors_config)\n"
"\n"
"# after\n"
"middleware = CORSMiddleware(allow_origins=cors_config.allow_origins, ...)\n"
"asgi_app = middleware(next_app)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:926
msgid ""
"The settings are copied on construction, so mutating ``CORSConfig`` after "
"the application has been created no longer affects the middleware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:960
msgid ""
"The ``litestar[testing]`` extra now installs `httpx2 <https://pydantic.dev/"
"docs/httpx2/>`_, the fork of ``httpx`` maintained by Pydantic, instead of "
"``httpx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:963
msgid ""
"``httpx2`` keeps the public API of ``httpx`` 0.28.1, but it is a distinct "
"module, so every ``httpx`` reference in a test suite has to be renamed, "
"including annotations such as ``response: httpx.Response``. Its exceptions "
"no longer inherit from the ``httpx`` ones, so an ``except httpx.HTTPError`` "
"around a test client call stops matching, silently where ``httpx`` remains "
"installed for other reasons. Beyond the rename:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:970
msgid ""
"``TestClient`` and ``AsyncTestClient`` now subclass ``httpx2.Client`` and "
"``httpx2.AsyncClient``, and ``subprocess_sync_client`` / "
"``subprocess_async_client`` return ``httpx2`` clients."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:973
msgid ""
"The logger is named ``httpx2``, which affects logging configuration and "
"``caplog`` assertions that reference the ``httpx`` logger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:975
msgid ""
"The clients inherit ``httpx2``'s ``sse()``, so ``httpx-sse`` is no longer "
"needed. The inherited ``websocket()`` does not work against the test "
"transport; use :meth:`~litestar.testing.TestClient.websocket_connect` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:978
msgid ""
"The subprocess clients send ``User-Agent: python-httpx2/<version>``; "
"``TestClient`` and ``AsyncTestClient`` keep sending ``testclient``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:980
msgid ""
"The extra pulls ``anyio>=4.10`` and ``idna>=3.18``, neither of which can be "
"satisfied alongside a lower pin, and verifies TLS against the operating "
"system trust store via ``truststore`` rather than ``certifi``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:984
msgid ""
"``httpx2.alias_httpx()``, which must run before anything imports ``httpx`` "
"or ``httpcore``, makes ``import httpx`` resolve to ``httpx2`` process-wide "
"for suites that cannot be renamed yet. Litestar never calls it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:989
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1005
msgid ":doc:`/usage/testing`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:996
msgid ""
"``httpx``, used by the test clients, has been moved from the default "
"dependencies to the ``litestar[testing]`` extra, which is included in "
"``litestar[full]``. The extra went on to replace ``httpx`` with ``httpx2`` "
"altogether, so 3.0 ships no dependency on ``httpx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1001
msgid ""
"Importing anything from ``litestar.testing`` without the extra installed now "
"raises a ``MissingDependencyException`` naming the extra to install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1012
msgid ""
"The ``litestar[cli]`` extra now requires ``rich-click>=1.9``. ``rich-click`` "
"was previously capped at ``<1.9``, which silently disabled the CLI's ``star-"
"box`` theme: the underlying ``theme`` option only exists from 1.9 onwards, "
"and assigning an unknown setting is ignored rather than raising."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1017
msgid ""
"The CLI configuration has been migrated off the options 1.9 deprecates "
"(``use_markdown`` / ``use_rich_markup`` in favour of ``text_markup``, and "
"``show_metavars_column`` / ``append_metavars_help`` in favour of "
"``options_table_column_types`` / ``options_table_help_sections``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1022
msgid ""
"The layout of the help output is preserved: option tables keep the long form "
"in the first column, the ``*`` marker on required parameters, and the "
"metavar appended directly after the help text. Colours do change, as the "
"``star-box`` theme now takes effect for the first time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1027
msgid ""
"This only affects applications that additionally pin ``rich-click<1.9`` "
"themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1031
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1047
msgid ":doc:`/usage/cli`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1038
msgid ""
"``click``, ``rich`` and ``rich-click``, which power the CLI, have been moved "
"from the default dependencies to the ``litestar[cli]`` extra. They remain "
"included in ``litestar[standard]`` and ``litestar[full]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1042
msgid ""
"Installing ``litestar`` on its own therefore no longer provides the "
"``litestar`` command. Invoking it without the extra now raises a "
"``MissingDependencyException`` naming the extra to install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1054
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib`` namespace. Integrations "
"previously available from this namespace have moved to their replacement "
"modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1062
msgid ""
"Remove declaring parameter and body metadata through default values and "
"setting defaults inside markers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1065
msgid ""
"The ``default`` keyword has been removed from ``Parameter`` and ``Body``, "
"along with the underlying ``KwargDefinition.default`` field. Passing it now "
"raises a ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1068
msgid ""
"Using a ``QueryParameter`` / ``HeaderParameter`` / ``PathParameter`` / "
"``CookieParameter`` or ``Body`` marker as a parameter *default value* (for "
"example ``data: Foo = Body(...)`` or ``param: int = QueryParameter(...)``) "
"now raises an exception"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1073
#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1100
msgid "**Migration**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1075
msgid ""
"If metadata is declared on the marker, move the marker into ``Annotated``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1077
msgid ""
"``data: Foo = Body(min_items=2)`` becomes ``data: Annotated[Foo, "
"Body(min_items=2)]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1078
msgid ""
"``param: int = QueryParameter(gt=1)`` becomes ``param: Annotated[int, "
"QueryParameter(gt=1)]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1080
msgid ""
"For the unconstrained case the dedicated markers can be used as a shorthand, "
"e.g. ``JSONBody[Foo]``, ``MsgPackBody[Foo]``, ``MultipartBody[Foo]`` or "
"``URLEncodedBody[Foo]`` for bodies, and ``FromQuery[int]``, "
"``FromHeader[int]``, ``FromCookie[int]`` or ``FromPath[int]`` for parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1085
msgid ""
"Hoist defaults set inside ``Annotated`` into the parameter default: ``param: "
"Annotated[int, QueryParameter(default=5)]`` becomes ``param: Annotated[int, "
"QueryParameter(...)] = 5``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1097
msgid ""
"Remove ``params.Dependency`` and ``params.DependencyKwarg`` that were "
"deprecated in ``2.23.0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1102
msgid "Replace ``foo: int = Dependency()`` with ``foo: NamedDependency[int]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1103
msgid ""
"Replace ``foo: Annotated[int, Dependency(default=1)]`` by hoisting the "
"default into the parameter default: ``foo: NamedDependency[int] = 1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1105
msgid ""
"Replace ``foo: Annotated[int, Dependency(skip_validation=True)`` with ``foo: "
"NamedDependency[SkipValidation[int]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1129
msgid "Drop support for Pydantic 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1131
msgid ""
"Pydantic 1 is no longer supported or tested against. No changes required for "
"applications already using Pydantic 2. Applications using Pydantic 1 or a "
"mix between 1 and 2 should upgrade to Pydantic 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1140
msgid ""
"Added optional ``ping_interval`` parameter to :class:`ServerSentEvent "
"<litestar.response.ServerSentEvent>` that sends SSE comment keepalive pings "
"at the specified interval to prevent connection timeouts from reverse "
"proxies or clients."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1150
msgid ""
"Remove Litestar's logging configuration, and related modules. In particular, "
"the following have been removed:"
